      "answer_exists": true,
      "candidate_performance": "Candidates performed well in (a)(i). Only a few candidates did not realise that the percentage error in measurement was being referred to and they answered 'easier to locate the positions of maxima as the dots are brighter'. Some candidates failed to find the correct values of θ or mistook the order of diffraction as n = 4 in (a)(iii). Weaker ones wrongly applied Δy = λD/a in this situation. In (b)(i), not many candidates knew that the equation Δy = λD/a could only be applied when λ ≪ a and a ≪ D. Some even thought that the equation was only applicable for light.",
